#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "REQUIRED logging, which is what drawing the call says. Logged before anything is written, so an install interrupted halfway is distinguishable from one never begun. A callActivity rather than a task: `log-message` is an independent sub-process, the second and last diagram in bootstrap. Any step may call it without being drawn; this one is drawn because here it is a step rather than a courtesy."
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The instructions belong to the harness being installed, not to bootstrap — bootstrap does not know what f-a-sci or smart-guidelines requires, and does not need to."
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "THE ONLY PROCESS IN BOOTSTRAP AN ACTOR STARTS. An Initiator that has read bootstrap/README.md is at its start event and has nowhere else to begin. The other diagrams here are not entry points and cannot be confused with this one: `log-message` is an independent SUB-PROCESS, called from a step and never started; `discussion` is entered from within this process when a fact is needed that no file holds — WHICH harness this should become and WHICH repositories are read from and written to, judgements no instruction body produces. PRECONDITION: the Initiator understands tasks, roles, processes, actors and skills, has been told it is an Initiator, and is at the start of this process. BPMN has no precondition element and this schema adds none yet, so it is stated here in the documentation and tracked as bean `lv3j`. NO folio:bean on any activity: a bean is work-plan machinery and an Initiator runs before the harness that carries it. isExecutable is false because the engine that runs a diagram is harness machinery too — this is data an Initiator reads, not a process bootstrap can drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only step needing a person, and the only place a judgement is made. IN, from the Initiator: a list of zero or more harnesses and a list of zero or more locations. OUT, from the Requestor: zero or ONE harness, and a list of zero or more locations. One at most — a list of two is not an answer, and the Initiator may not break the tie itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:105
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Three ways in, and all are logged rather than retried: no harness was chosen, a location is ALREADY initialized, or the instructions were not at the predetermined spot. Guessing a harness produces a repository set up as the wrong thing, which is worse than one not set up at all. \"Already initialized\" is a failure of THIS process and not a fault in the repository — the usual case is that the work is done. It ends here because the alternative is re-initialising over an instance that already has content, history and dependents, and the damage from that is not recoverable by running anything again. What the Requestor does next — upgrade it, initialise elsewhere, or nothing — is a new decision, and a new decision starts at A_ConfirmHarness rather than being taken by an Initiator that has just been told to stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:121
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Zero or more. Is this a git repository already, or were one or more URLs to repositories supplied? Both are Knowledge Graph Data Stores; the difference is only how they are reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../bootstrap/workflows/initialize-harness.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Zero or more. The DEFAULT is bootstrap itself. Context may name others — \"please initialize litlfred/folio-assistant\" in a discussion is one, and so is a derivative such as cat-harness or smart-guidelines. This step narrows; it does not decide."
msgstr ""
